    "text": "1 days ago DUBLIN, Ga. — The school bells have gone quiet for the summer, but inside Dublin City Schools' board office, the work is anything but over. Nearly a year after the district's budget deficit came to light, school leaders are racing against the calendar — trying to rebuild broken finances, restore frayed public trust, and fill two of the most critical leadership seats in the district before students return in August. Read full article",
